    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nOn the math section of the SAT exam, you may be asked to find the solution to a one-step multiplication equation and evaluate an expression once you've found the solution.\n\nContent:\nMake sure you double-check your arithmetic before submitting your answer! This is especially important for free-response questions.\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Solving One-Step Multiplication Equations\n\nExample Prompt:\n[MATH: 2v = 38]\nWhat value of [MATH: v] is the solution to the given equation?\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 2v = 38] and are asked to solve for [MATH: v.]\n\nLet's solve the equation for [MATH: v{:}]\n\n[MATH: 2v|= 38; v|= (38)/(2); v|= 19]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: v] that satisfies the equation is [MATH: 19.]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 4x = 60]\nWhat value of [MATH: x] is the solution to the given equation?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 18]\nb. [MATH: 12]\nc. [MATH: 20]\nd. [MATH: 10]\ne. [MATH: 15]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: 2v = 38]\nWhat value of [MATH: v] is the solution to the given equation?\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 15]\nb. [MATH: 19]\nc. [MATH: 20]\nd. [MATH: 21]\ne. [MATH: 23]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Solving a One-Step Multiplication Equation and Evaluating an Expression\n\nExample Prompt:\nIf [MATH: 11k = 77,] what is the value of [MATH: 6k?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 11k = 77] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: 6k.]\n\nFirst, we solve the equation for [MATH: k{:}]\n[MATH: 11k|= 77; k|= (77)/(11); k|= 7]\n\nNow, we substitute [MATH: k = 7] into the expression [MATH: 6k] and simplify:\n[MATH: 6k|= 6 \u22c5 7; = 42]\n\nSo, the value of [MATH: 6k] is [MATH: 42.]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 4x = 16,] what is the value of [MATH: 9x?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 36]\nb. [MATH: 32]\nc. [MATH: 64]\nd. [MATH: 20]\ne. [MATH: 144]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 11k = 77,] what is the value of [MATH: 6k?]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 36]\nb. [MATH: 42]\nc. [MATH: 48]\nd. [MATH: 45]\ne. [MATH: 40]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Solving a One-Step Multiplication Equation and Evaluating an Expression (Free-Response)\n\nExample Prompt:\nCalculate [MATH: m + 4] given that [MATH: 8m = 64.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe are given the equation [MATH: 8m = 64] and are asked to find the value of [MATH: m + 4.]\n\nTo isolate the variable [MATH: m,] we divide both sides of the equation by [MATH: 8]:\n[MATH: m|= (64)/(8); = 8]\n\nNow, we substitute [MATH: m = 8] into [MATH: m + 4] and simplify:\n[MATH: m + 4|= 8 + 4; = 12]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 5x = 35,] then [MATH: 7x =][FREE_ENTRY 1].\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nIf [MATH: 8n = 24,] then [MATH: n + 5 =][FREE_ENTRY 1]."
